From 0acb4310b3e861d19472be5587069f62766143a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jmestwa-coder <jmestwa@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:16:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] imap: bound STATUS mailbox literal read in
 cmd_parse_status (#5045)

cmd_parse_status() advances past a STATUS mailbox name sent as an IMAP
literal with `s = mailbox + litlen; s[0] = 0; s++; SKIPWS(s)`, even when
the literal exactly fills the continuation line. A server that sends the
mailbox name with no trailing ` (items)` makes the read step past the end
of the response, so the following `(` check and item loop parse leftover
bytes of the reused buffer as STATUS values. Guard the advance like the
sibling cmd_parse_list() already does.

(cherry picked from commit 8793720ddf1c7cfc190378c41b89daa67a6d7d45)
---
 imap/command.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/imap/command.c b/imap/command.c
index 3d992c4..0d0b135 100644
--- a/imap/command.c
+++ b/imap/command.c
@@ -923,9 +923,12 @@ static void cmd_parse_status(struct ImapAccountData *adata, char *s)
 
     mailbox = adata->buf;
     s = mailbox + litlen;
-    s[0] = '\0';
-    s++;
-    SKIPWS(s);
+    if (s[0] != '\0')
+    {
+      s[0] = '\0';
+      s++;
+      SKIPWS(s);
+    }
   }
   else
   {
